00:25:22.020 --> 00:25:25.190
So a product is nothing more
than a collection of APIs,

00:25:25.190 --> 00:25:28.290
maybe sub-resources within
an API, maybe just one API.

00:25:28.290 --> 00:25:31.760
And basically, it's the way
within Apigee's API management

00:25:31.760 --> 00:25:34.900
to select what the app is
allowed to actually access.

00:25:34.900 --> 00:25:36.358
And why do we call it a product?

00:25:36.358 --> 00:25:38.900
Well, we've found that companies
that are the most successful

00:25:38.900 --> 00:25:41.990
with their API programs, they
treat their APIs like products.

00:25:41.990 --> 00:25:43.030
What does that mean?

00:25:43.030 --> 00:25:44.360
They have a product manager.

00:25:44.360 --> 00:25:46.110
They use outside in thinking.

00:25:46.110 --> 00:25:48.977
So they develop their APIs
with the API consumer in mind.

00:25:48.977 --> 00:25:50.810
They don't just say,
hey, I've got a system.

00:25:50.810 --> 00:25:51.860
It's got six fields.

00:25:51.860 --> 00:25:54.500
I'm going to expose those six
fields, and that's my API.

00:25:54.500 --> 00:25:59.930
So just some important concepts
and in terms of API management.

